30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings are a bit worrying. The roads north of the river closed several times last winter, though the community halls stayed open.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that the outer wards lost their bus links. Now, some residents face an hour's trip just to reach a staffed counter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that a digitisation project from six years ago was a mess—half the images weren't indexed! But some evening groups are still going strong.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"As I feared, the funding is precarious. The county grant only covers session fees for a year, and last year's vehicle costs overran significantly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We have a gap in expertise. We have retired tradespeople volunteering, but no one on the payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, it seems our neighbors in the north are quite isolated. If the buses are gone and the roads close, they are truly cut off.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, exactly. And my data shows that while our rooms are full in the evening, people are using the catalogue from home long after we lock up.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, does that mean we can't do things with outside teachers? I saw that the partner-run groups from six years ago are the only ones that lasted!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the longevity of those groups is interesting, but @Minako's point about supervision is key. We cannot fund what we cannot manage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, and we must consider the tools. We have volunteers for repairs, but the person who certified the power tools retired in the spring.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It feels as though we are describing a community that is eager for help but blocked by distance and a lack of official support.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Any expansion that requires people to travel to the main branch will likely fail the very people who need us most.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"So we need something that goes to them! But it has to be better than the old digitisation project, or it'll just be a waste.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, a mobile service would address the distance, but my records show vehicle costs are already spiraling. We must be cautious of the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"A mobile service also requires staff. If we don't have the supervisors or the certified technicians, we are just adding more stress to the roster.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
